### CropGuard API - sample requests
### Works in VS Code with the REST Client extension, or copy the curl versions below.

### Health check
GET http://localhost:5000/api/health

### Analyze a crop image (replace the path with a real photo)
# curl -X POST http://localhost:5000/api/analyze \
#   -F "image=@./sample-data/tomato-leaf.jpg" \
#   -F "crop=Tomato" \
#   -F "stage=Flowering" \
#   -F "save=true"

### Full library
GET http://localhost:5000/api/library

### Diseases only
GET http://localhost:5000/api/diseases

### Pests only
GET http://localhost:5000/api/pests

### Search the library
GET http://localhost:5000/api/library?search=tomato

### One entry
GET http://localhost:5000/api/library/early-blight

### History
GET http://localhost:5000/api/history?limit=20

### Dashboard numbers
GET http://localhost:5000/api/history/stats

### Save a record by hand (body taken from sample-history.json)
POST http://localhost:5000/api/history
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "crop": "Tomato",
  "detection": "Early Blight",
  "detectionKey": "early-blight",
  "type": "disease",
  "confidence": 94,
  "severity": "Medium",
  "severityScore": 58
}

### Delete a record
# DELETE http://localhost:5000/api/history/<id>
